  "ready": true,
  "readyNote": "re-measured 11/10/2026 with the per-element probe on quickstart/ja-space/j6 1.0.3 (published; tasks/evidence/ds-remeasure-5-2026-10-11/ja-space): 12/12 with Moxie, MotherDuck, Toggl Track, Apple, controls 0 differences, no text made less readable than the template's own, 73%–100% of the page follows; checked by eye under Moxie and Toggl Track (dark), MotherDuck and Apple (light). The older probe passed it while its contrast kinds found no element on the home page (only the footer was measured); measured on the sections themselves, the header and the hero on the dark photo turned grey/dark under the light systems (hero lead, logo, active menu item: 1.04–2.07): both are kept (keepScopes + keepColors), faces still follow. The body probe reads the feature cards' running text (the hero lead keeps its own 400); the footer's .text-hide \"Powered by\" link (font-size 0) is no longer judged (flow.mjs). Re-measured 12/10/2026 with the unified probe (fix/ds-reverify-d) on the published 1.0.3, three runs: 12/12 each, controls 0 differences, 73%–100% of the page follows, no text made less readable than the template's own; the muted and body kinds at 1440 px live only in sections JA Space reveals through jQuery inview (opacity 0 until .ja-inview, from 992 px), which the measuring browser's page walk does not always trigger, so one desktop view had no sample in two of the three runs (MotherDuck, then Toggl Track) and every view had samples in the other; the contract is unchanged (tasks/evidence/ds-reverify-d-2026-10-12/ja-space)",
