  "sideNote": "14/10/2026 (visual review, round 3): project captions. On /our-projects each card’s title and type (.view-project .intro-wrap, white words with a faint black shadow, laid on the bottom 104px of a pastel photo) took the system’s display weight, so a thin face (Playfair 400 under Mailchimp, Inter Tight 300 under Stripe) left white hairlines on a light photo — already a weak pairing in the template (bold 700 white on pastel). The caption block gets a black scrim rising from the card’s foot (65% → 50% → none) and the title keeps the template’s 700, the type its 400: the words stay the template’s white on its photo, now on a ground dark enough for them. On the home carousel (.latest-project) the hover caption sits on the accent gradient overlay but was set in the system’s heading ink (the template’s fg-2, white in its own palette): it takes the accent’s own words (accent-on, followRules), and the overlay runs accent → accent-hover instead of ending in the template’s literal coral #f55d59",
  "literalsNote": "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65) / 0.5: the scrim under the project captions’ white words on their photos (/our-projects) — the template’s own black (its 30% black text shadow), deepened so its white words read on a light photo",
  "reviewV8Note": "15/10/2026 (look review v8): the client logos are white pictures made for the dark page: under a light system they are inverted; the grid lines take the soft line colour (the template’s hairline on black)",
  "hoverNote": "21/10/2026 (HOVER-1 and HOVER-2, TEXT-1 batch 1): each state reads a role apart from rest. The header is kept, so every --ds-c-* is reset inside it: the logo's hover read var(--ds-c-accent-on-ink), found nothing and inherited the header's #9e9e9e, 2.7:1 on the Home Light page's white header (HOVER-1); there (.itemid-128) the logo and 'Start a Project' hover in a role read on the body, outside the reset (--tracy-light-header-hover): the system's text under a light system (4.71:1 or more on #fcfcfc and white across the 1028 light systems of the library), the system's page 40% toward white under a dark one (black's #666666: 5.7:1 on the white, 3.66:1 on black), 21/10/2026: the header sits on the hero photo's white, but the hover probe sees no photo there, only the dark page behind it, so the state must read on both (3:1 or more on #fcfcfc under 1332 of the 1334 dark sides of the library, on their page under 1330; the page 40% toward black read 1:1 on that page, HOVER-1 on 'Start a Project'; the template's own red #eb4c49 is the template's brand hue on a hover, ACCENT-LEAK; filling the header with the photo's #fcfcfc was measured as a kept block and its 'Start a Project' rest as low text, TPL-1 and CON-2). On the dark pages the menu keeps the template's own words (80% white at rest, white on hover, focus and when active or open): the band's second text is judged on the recorded black, not the photo, and read 4.08 to 4.3:1 on it under every system of the library (CON-1 on Moxie, 4.38:1 against the template's 7.4:1), so hover and focus are told apart by an underline instead. 'Start a Project' turns from the band's accent to its text. The home carousel's caption (shown on hover only) reads the page text at rest and the accent's words on hover, so the hover differs in colour as well as in opacity, which the probe does not read on the words. Pagination links take the neutral hover ground under the page text, as Bootstrap's own hover. 21/10/2026 (review): 'Start a Project' turns from the band's accent to its text, the same white under 466 systems, so its hover and focus also underline, as do the pagination links (their rest words are not a role this contract writes); the carousel caption, hidden at rest, reads the accent words at rest (apart from accent-on under every system, where the page text was the same under 3). 21/10/2026 (measure of batch 1): the Home Light alias was written on .itemid-128, a class of <html> itself, which a rule under :root never names: it was never set and the logo's hover fell back to an inherited grey (#9e9e9e on white under 5fd3, HOVER-1); it is set on the body (body:is(.itemid-128 *)). The logo's hover reads the page text, within 3 channels of its kept #333 rest under eight systems, so it underlines too; the project cards' titles (.latest-project) show on the card's own :hover, which the hover probe never reaches from the link, so the link's state underlines them (HOVER-2 on the three home pages)."
}
